<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Range — a parabola in vertex form</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Consider the function \( f(x) = {@fdisp@} \).</p>
<p>State the range of \(f\) as an inequality in \(y\).</p>
<div>\(y\) [[input:ans_sym]] [[validation:ans_sym]] [[input:ans_val]] [[validation:ans_val]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt_sym]] [[feedback:prt_val]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>In <strong>vertex form</strong> \(f(x)=a(x-h)^2+k\), the point \((h,k)\) is the vertex of the parabola. Here \(f(x) = {@fdisp@}\), so the vertex is \(({@h@},{@k@})\). Since a square is never negative, \({@(x-h)^2@} \geq 0\) for every \(x\), with equality only at \(x={@h@}\).</p>
<ul>
<li>If \(a &gt; 0\), the parabola opens <strong>upward</strong> and the vertex is a <strong>minimum</strong>: the range is \(y \geq k\).</li>
<li>If \(a &lt; 0\), the parabola opens <strong>downward</strong> and the vertex is a <strong>maximum</strong>: the range is \(y \leq k\).</li>
</ul>
<p>Here \(a={@a@}\), so the range is \({@range_ineq@}\).</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Graph of the parabola y = f(x) with its vertex marked and a dashed horizontal line through the vertex.">
[[jsxgraph width="320px" height="220px"]]
(function() {
  var a = {#a#};
  var h = {#h#};
  var k = {#k#};
  var board = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {
    boundingbox: [h - 5, {#ytop#}, h + 5, {#ybot#}],
    axis: true, grid: false,
    showNavigation: false, showCopyright: false
  });
  board.create('functiongraph', [function(x) { return a * (x - h) * (x - h) + k; }], {strokeColor: '#003399', strokeWidth: 2});
  board.create('line', [[h - 5, k], [h + 5, k]], {strokeColor: '#cc0000', dash: 2, strokeWidth: 1, fixed: true});
  board.create('point', [h, k], {size: 4, color: '#cc0000', fixed: true, name: 'vertex', label: {offset: [10, a > 0 ? -15 : 15], anchorX: 'left'}});
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
